{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>יִרֶה יָרֹה — he shall be stoned or shot.</b> From here [we learn] for those stoned, that they are cast down from the place of stoning, which was two stories high (Sanhedrin 45)." "<b>יָרֹה — shot.</b> Cast down below to the ground, as in ״יָרָה בַיָּם״." "<b>When the ram's horn sounds long.</b> When the yovel draws out a long sound — it is the sign of the withdrawal of the Shekhinah and the cessation of the voice; and once it withdraws, they are permitted to ascend." "<b>The yovel.</b> It is the shofar of a ram, for in Arabic they call a ram yuvla, and it was the shofar of a ram of Isaac's (Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 31)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:08.457380175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}